course: dictionary
lesson: 2574
title: Big words about the brain
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are about illnesses, and they can sound hard to say. Dementia is one of them. You can work it out from the words around it. «Some old people get an illness of the brain called dementia» tells you it is an illness, that it affects the brain, and that it often happens to older people.
explain: Look for clues in the rest of the sentence. «It makes them forget, even the names of people they love» shows what dementia does: it takes memories away. Try your meaning in the sentence. An illness of the brain that makes people forget still makes sense, so you are on the right track.
explain: Some sentences also show how people feel. «It is the illness forgetting, not the love going away.» Dementia takes away memories and words, but the love stays. A person with dementia still needs patience and kindness.
fact: Dementia is an illness of the brain, most common in old people.
fact: It slowly makes it hard to remember things, think clearly, find words and look after yourself.
fact: Dementia is not the fault of the person who has it, and it is not catching.
fact: Alzheimer's disease is the most common kind of dementia.
fact: Children can help by being patient, speaking calmly and kindly, and looking at old photos together.
exercise: «Dementia is an illness of the brain that makes people forget, more and more over time.» What does dementia make people do? | Sleep only in the day | Hear sounds better | Grow taller every year | *Forget more and more over time
exercise: «People with dementia often repeat themselves.» What does repeat themselves mean? | Forget their own name just once | *Say the same thing again and again | Go to sleep early every night | Read a book aloud
exercise: Nadia says, «Dementia is catching, so stay away from grandparents.» What is the right answer? | *No, dementia is not catching, and it is not anyone's fault | Yes, you can catch it from a cold hug | Yes, keep your distance from every grandparent | It only happens to children
test: «Some old people get an illness of the brain called dementia that makes them forget, even the names of people they love.» What does this sentence tell you? | *Dementia makes people forget, even people they love | It only happens in stories | It is a kind of toothache | Dementia makes people grow taller
test: Your grandad with dementia asks the same question three times. What helps most? | Arguing and saying «you told me» each time | Telling him he is silly | Ignoring him until he stops | *Answering patiently and kindly, perhaps looking at old photos together
exam: Which word means an illness of the brain that makes it hard to remember and think clearly? | Curt | Barely | Treacherous | *Dementia
